# The Vercel build only needs ui/ (source + the committed static-api JSON) and vercel.json. Everything
# else is the Python agent, its 225 MB scoring database, and local envs: irrelevant to a static build
# and past Vercel's 100 MB per-file limit.
#
# Every path here is root-anchored with a leading slash. An unanchored "cases/" matches a directory of
# that name at ANY depth, which silently excluded ui/public/static-api/cases/ and shipped a site whose
# case detail and subgraph endpoints all 404'd.
/.venv/
/.git/
/node_modules/
/ui/node_modules/
/ui/dist/

/data/
/cases/
/outputs/
/mcp/
/scripts/
/tests/
/notebooks/

/api/
/agent/
/detectors/
/graphrag/
/tigergraph/

# Vercel's framework detection reads pyproject.toml at the root and concludes this is a FastAPI
# backend, which overrides the static build entirely.
/pyproject.toml
/Makefile
/Dockerfile
/.dockerignore

*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.parquet
*.tsv
*.joblib
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.env
.env.local
.tg_token
